Call site of io.ReadAll(f) on an *os.File inside Slurp (whose declaration set is all
Unresolved, see slurp_named_result_defer_close; the call site itself is analysable).
io.ReadAll turns io.EOF into nil: expected the (*os.File).Read set WITHOUT io.EOF:
os.ErrInvalid, and the poll/syscall read errors under *fs.PathError.Unwrap (os.ErrClosed
replacing poll.ErrFileClosing there), plus their unwrapped copies (the accepted
(*os.File).wrapErr over-approximation, see README). No "source: read: %w" link.
